# Redoubt disable-157-cloud-features.patch: four Firefox 157 features that send
# browsing data to Mozilla or Google services, off for good on Android.
#
# Owner decision 2026-10-02 (docs/android/TRACK.md, "Decision reversed"),
# taken when Android moved to Firefox release 157. Each switch is a constant,
# not a default, so neither Nimbus (stubbed by no-nimbus.patch), a stale
# SharedPreferences value from an earlier build nor Secret Settings can turn
# it back on.
#
# 1. Shake to Summarize -- fenix utils/Settings.kt
#    shakeToSummarizeFeatureFlagEnabled is false. Summaries are produced by
#    Mozilla's MLPA service (lib-llm-mlpa, MlpaConfig.prodProd =
#    mlpa-prod-prod-mozilla.freetls.fastly.net) from the page text. Every
#    surface reads this flag: Components.aiFeatureRegistry registers
#    PageSummaryFeature only when it is true; FenixSummarizationFeatureConfiguration
#    .isFeatureAvailable gates canShowFeature, which gates the menu item, its
#    highlight, the toolbar CFR, the toolbar highlight and
#    BrowserFragment.setupShakeDetection (no accelerometer listener is
#    registered); SettingsFragment and CustomizationFragment hide the
#    summarize settings. The only code that reaches MLPA is
#    SummarizationFragment (components.llm.mlpaProvider), which is opened only
#    from those surfaces. :components:lib-llm-mlpa stays in the dependency
#    graph: Llm.kt, ClientUUID.kt, FenixMlpaService.kt and the debug drawer's
#    IntegrityTools all import it, so dropping it is a source removal across
#    five files, not a build.gradle line -- left for a follow-up.
#
# 2. IP Protection ("Built-in VPN", Mozilla's hosted proxy) -- Settings.kt,
#    FenixApplication.kt, components/ipprotection/IPProtection.kt,
#    home/intent/HomeDeepLinkIntentProcessor.kt
#    isIPProtectionAvailable is false, so IPProtectionPromptRepository never
#    shows the onboarding sheet. FenixApplication no longer calls
#    maybeSetupIPProtection(), so IPProtectionFeature.initialize() and the
#    storage synchronizer never run. IPProtection.eligibilityStorage is a
#    constant Ineligible instead of FenixIPProtectionEligibilityStorage (Nimbus,
#    home region, Secret Settings override); with no Eligible state the
#    settings row (SettingsFragment.setupIPProtectionPreferences:
#    isVisible = state.isEligible), the menu and trust-panel entries stay
#    hidden. The settings_ip_protection deep link is unmapped.
#
# 3. Merino shortcut icons -- Settings.kt, home/topsites/store/PopularSite.kt
#    enableAddShortcutsImprovement (Nimbus add-shortcuts-improvement) is false,
#    so neither the "Add shortcut" tile nor its popular-sites sheet appears.
#    Independently, ManifestEntry.toPopularSite() drops the manifest's icon URL
#    (prod-images.merino.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net), so a popular site can
#    never make that request even if a future surface shows the list.
#    BrowserIcons' MerinoManifestIconPreparer was already removed (LW-M4-10).
#
# 4. Google Lens -- Settings.kt
#    googleLensIntegrationEnabled is false in every build type. LensFeature,
#    LensSearchActivity (via SearchWidgetProvider), the toolbar Lens button,
#    the image context menu entry (FenixApplication's googleLensEnabled) and
#    SearchEngineFragment's preference all check it; LensImageUploader, the
#    only code that posts to lens.google.com/upload, is constructed only behind
#    those checks.
#
# The three flags that were preference-backed keep a setter, as a no-op, so
# that upstream callers (androidTest helpers, unit tests) still compile. Their
# Secret Settings switches are removed (fragment and xml), together with the
# IP Protection override switch, which only fed the two decisions above.
#
# Tests: FenixSummarizationFeatureConfigurationTest and
# IPProtectionPromptRepositoryTest tested the behaviour this patch removes
# and are deleted; HomeDeepLinkIntentProcessorTest's settings_ip_protection
# case now asserts that nothing is navigated to; LibreWolfCloudFeaturesTest
# pins all four constants, every summarize discovery surface, the IP
# Protection prompt and the Merino icon strip.
#
# Applies last in android.txt, on top of no-gms.patch, no-glean.patch and
# firefox-suggest-policy.patch, which also edit SecretSettingsFragment.kt and
# Settings.kt (check-patch-order.py records the pairs).
#
# 158 rebase (2026-10-04, pre-rebase against Firefox 158.0b3): no change of
# intent. The Settings.kt shakeToSummarizeFeatureFlagEnabled hunk needed fuzz 2
# on 158 (the new tabReloadCover settings follow it), so the patch is
# regenerated at fuzz 0 on the in-order 158 tree.
#
# 158.0b4 (2026-10-06): no change of intent. 158.0b4 removed the IP
# Protection "locations" secret setting (its SecretSettingsFragment.kt block
# and Settings.isIPProtectionLocationsEnabled), which was the trailing context
# of the SecretSettingsFragment.kt IP Protection hunk and of the Settings.kt
# isIPProtectionAvailable hunk. The first rejected on b4 and the second needed
# fuzz 1. Both were regenerated at fuzz 0 on the in-order 158.0b4 tree; the
# removed and added lines are unchanged. This text no longer applies to b3.
